{"ref":"BDB, אֻמָּה","hw":"אֻמָּה","html":"† <big>[<span dir=\"rtl\">אֻמָּה</span>]</big>  <strong>n.f. tribe, people (</strong>Arabic <span dir=\"rtl\">أُمَّةٌ</span>; Assyrian <em>ummatu</em> cf. Jen<sup>Kosmol. 336</sup>, Aramaic <span dir=\"rtl\">ܐܘܽܡܬܳܐ</span>, <span dir=\"rtl\">אוּמָּא</span><strong>)</strong> only pl. <span dir=\"rtl\">אֻמּוֹת</span> <a data-ref=\"Numbers 25:15\" href=\"/Numbers.25.15\">Nu 25:15</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">אֻמִּים</span> <a data-ref=\"Psalms 117:1\" href=\"/Psalms.117.1\">ψ 117:1</a>; sf. <span dir=\"rtl\">אֻמֹּתָם</span> <a data-ref=\"Genesis 25:16\" href=\"/Genesis.25.16\">Gn 25:16</a>;—of tribes of Ishmaelites <a data-ref=\"Genesis 25:16\" href=\"/Genesis.25.16\">Gn 25:16</a>; of Midian (‖ <span dir=\"rtl\">בֵּית־אָב</span>) <a data-ref=\"Numbers 25:15\" href=\"/Numbers.25.15\">Nu 25:15</a>; ‖ <span dir=\"rtl\">גּוֹיִם</span> <a data-ref=\"Psalms 117:1\" href=\"/Psalms.117.1\">ψ 117:1</a>.","next":"BDB, אֲמָם","prev":"BDB, אַמָּה⁵"}